-- title:
--   Slices of a flat pushout along a triple fibre product
-- statement:
--   Fix commutative rings $B$, $B_1$, $B'$, $M$, $N$ in a single universe, together with algebra structures $B\to B_1$, $B'\to B_1$, $B\to B'$, $B\to M$, $B'\to N$, $M\to N$, $B\to N$, the two scalar-tower compatibilities for $B\subseteq B'\subseteq N$ and $B\subseteq M\subseteq N$, the hypothesis `Algebra.IsPushout B B' M N` (so that $N$ realises the pushout $M\otimes_B B'$), and flatness of $M$ as a $B$-module. Assume further: $B\to B_1$ is surjective (`hπ`); three $B$-algebra maps $p_0,p_1,p_2\colon B'\to B$ are given, all lying over the map $B'\to B_1$ (`hp`), jointly injective (`hinj`), and jointly surjective onto those triples $(b_i)$ in $B$ whose images in $B_1$ agree pairwise (`hsurj`); and three $B$-algebra maps $e_0,e_1,e_2\colon N\to M$ are given which restrict to the identity along $M\to N$ and to $p_i$ along $B'\to N$. The conclusion is the conjunction of two assertions: the $e_i$ jointly separate points of $N$, and every triple $(m_0,m_1,m_2)$ in $M$ with all differences $m_i-m_j$ lying in the ideal of $M$ generated by the image of $\ker(B\to B_1)$ is of the form $(e_0 n,e_1 n,e_2 n)$ for some $n\in N$.
--
--   This is the flat base-change statement that a pushout along a triple fibre product $B'\cong B\times_{B_1}B\times_{B_1}B$ is recovered by its three slices, with image exactly the triples congruent modulo $JM$, where $J=\ker(B\to B_1)$; it is the ring-theoretic input behind the Schlessinger-type gluing conditions for deformation functors. It is used to produce and to compare algebra maps out of such a pushout, in [`Algebra.IsPushout.exists_algHom_slice_eq_of_flat`](thm.html#Algebra.IsPushout.exists_algHom_slice_eq_of_flat), [`Algebra.IsPushout.exists_algEquiv_slice_eq_of_flat`](thm.html#Algebra.IsPushout.exists_algEquiv_slice_eq_of_flat) and [`GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.eq_of_forall_slice_comp_eq`](thm.html#GoodReductionJacobian.BareDeformation.eq_of_forall_slice_comp_eq).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_Algebra_IsPushout_slice_ext_and_exists_of_flat.lean

import Mathlib

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

set_option autoImplicit false

open TensorProduct

universe u

theorem Algebra.IsPushout.slice_ext_and_exists_of_flat
    {B B₁ B' M N : Type u} [CommRing B] [CommRing B₁] [CommRing B'] [CommRing M] [CommRing N]
    [Algebra B B₁] [Algebra B' B₁] [Algebra B B'] [Algebra B M] [Algebra B' N] [Algebra M N] [Algebra B N]
    [IsScalarTower B B' N] [IsScalarTower B M N] [Algebra.IsPushout B B' M N] [Module.Flat B M]
    (hπ : Function.Surjective (algebraMap B B₁))
    (p : Fin 3 → (B' →ₐ[B] B))
    (hp : ∀ (i : Fin 3) (x : B'), algebraMap B B₁ (p i x) = algebraMap B' B₁ x)
    (hinj : ∀ x y : B', (∀ i, p i x = p i y) → x = y)
    (hsurj : ∀ b : Fin 3 → B, (∀ i j, algebraMap B B₁ (b i) = algebraMap B B₁ (b j)) → ∃ x : B', ∀ i, p i x = b i)
    (e : Fin 3 → (N →ₐ[B] M))
    (heM : ∀ (i : Fin 3) (m : M), e i (algebraMap M N m) = m)
    (heB : ∀ (i : Fin 3) (x : B'), e i (algebraMap B' N x) = algebraMap B M (p i x)) :
    (∀ n n' : N, (∀ i, e i n = e i n') → n = n') ∧
    (∀ m : Fin 3 → M, (∀ i j, m i - m j ∈ (RingHom.ker (algebraMap B B₁)).map (algebraMap B M)) →
      ∃ n : N, ∀ i, e i n = m i) := by sorry
